\section{Introduction}

Statistics plays an important role in government administration. It provides information for planning, policy formulation, resource allocation and evaluation of development programmes. Statistical departments collect, analyse and publish economic, social, demographic and environmental data.

In India, the major central institution responsible for official statistics is the \textbf{Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation (MoSPI)}. At the state level, the \textbf{Department of Economics and Statistics (DES), Government of Kerala} performs major statistical functions.

%================================================
% GOVERNMENT OF INDIA
%================================================

\section{Statistical Activities under the Government of India}

MoSPI is the nodal ministry for the organized development of India's statistical system. Its activities are mainly carried out through the National Statistical Office and other divisions.

The major activities and functions include:

\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
    \item Conducting sample surveys on employment, consumption, health, education and socio-economic subjects.
    
    \item Preparing National Accounts Statistics, including GDP, GVA and related indicators.
    
    \item Compiling price statistics such as the Consumer Price Index (CPI).
    
    \item Preparing industrial statistics, including IIP and ASI.
    
    \item Producing labour and employment statistics through the Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS).
    
    \item Developing indicators for monitoring Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).
    
    \item Disseminating statistical reports and datasets.
    
    \item Monitoring selected government programmes and infrastructure projects.
\end{itemize}

These activities provide quantitative evidence for national planning and public policy.

%================================================
% GOVERNMENT OF KERALA
%================================================

\section{Statistical Activities under the Government of Kerala}

The \textbf{Department of Economics and Statistics (DES), Government of Kerala} is the nodal agency for official statistics in the state. It collects and analyses data required for state planning and development.

The major activities and functions include:

\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
    \item Preparing State Income Statistics, including GSDP, GVA and per-capita income.
    
    \item Collecting agricultural statistics on crop area, production, yield and land utilisation through activities such as EARAS.
    
    \item Collecting price statistics, including retail prices and consumer price indices.
    
    \item Preparing industrial statistics through IIP and ASI.
    
    \item Collecting population and vital statistics, including births and deaths.
    
    \item Conducting and participating in National Sample Surveys on employment, household expenditure, health and education.
    
    \item Compiling labour and housing statistics.
    
    \item Providing local-level statistics for district, municipality and panchayat planning.
\end{itemize}

