\section{Importance of Government Statistics}

Government statistics supports budgeting, employment planning, agricultural development, industrial policy, welfare programmes and infrastructure development.

Mathematical methods such as sampling, estimation, averages, variance, index numbers, correlation and regression are widely used. Thus, statistical departments provide an important practical application of mathematics and statistics.

%================================================
% CONCLUSION
%================================================

\section{Conclusion}

The statistical departments of India and Kerala support evidence-based governance. MoSPI produces national statistics, while DES performs similar functions at the state level, with emphasis on agriculture, state income, local statistics and socio-economic conditions.

Reliable statistics enables governments to identify development needs, formulate policies and measure outcomes. Thus, statistical departments connect mathematical analysis with government administration and social development.

